{
 "_doc": "Zang's movement vocabulary (ported from ZingAIStack config/gestures.json; Zing library-clip variants removed because Zang has no recorded action library yet: dropped gestures = salute, dab). Arm poses are [shoulder pitch, shoulder roll, elbow] in anatomical degrees (pitch+ forward/up, roll+ outward, elbow+ folds inward; co-speech limits pitch -15..170, roll -8..100, elbow 0..109, head pan +-30). Each gesture has trigger words (EN + Hinglish), hf = Hugging Face gesture classes mapped to it, and a list of visually different VARIANTS; the planner picks one per use and never repeats the last one, so <think> is think1, think2, think3... in turn (the LLM can also force one: <think2>). Variant fields: arms r|l|both|either (either = whichever hand is free, head mirrors), pose (pose_l for an asymmetric two-hand pose), hold s, prep s, head pan deg, head_osc [[dt, deg],...] pan pulses, osc {joint, values, period, cycles} = oscillate one joint, path {poses, period} = move through extra poses, sway [..] = weight-shift pulses (-1..1), action = replay a Plode library action, min_arousal (+ fallback gesture). Poses are collision-projected against the URDF meshes at runtime; tests/test_core.py checks that all variants stay visually distinct. Rhymes, songs and stories use the specific gestures (down, away, rain, sun, round, fly, sleep, clap, run, music): the LLM writes the tag, the engine picks the variant. ZANG MAPPING: arm poses are retargeted to Zang joints by zang_ai.robot (anatomical signs derived from the MJCF at load). Zang has NO head: 'head'/'head_osc' degrees drive a gaze turn of the waist (waist_yaw) scaled by config/motion.json gaze.gain and clamped to its co-speech range. 'sway' drives hip_roll/ankle_roll weight shift like Zing.",
